WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.579 --> 00:00:05.199
- Your hunger will drive you every day.

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:06.219
- Hunger.

00:00:06.219 --> 00:00:07.229
- The main thing, hunger.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:08.128
- Hungry.

00:00:08.128 --> 00:00:09.075
- Hungry.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.479
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:12.912
Today we're going to talk
about how you can be hungry.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.904
And as always, guys, as
you're watching the videos,

00:00:14.904 --> 00:00:16.679
if you see something that really resonates

00:00:16.679 --> 00:00:18.707
with you, please leave
it in the comments below.

00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:20.133
And put quotes around it, so other people

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.431
can be inspired.

00:00:21.431 --> 00:00:22.681
And if you write it down,

00:00:22.681 --> 00:00:26.231
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself, as well.

00:00:26.231 --> 00:00:28.814
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:39.240
- When you think about life,
everybody wants the prize,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.111
but nobody wants the process.

00:00:41.111 --> 00:00:42.263
Everybody wants the championship

00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:43.931
but nobody wants the day to day.

00:00:43.931 --> 00:00:45.132
Everybody wants to win games.

00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:46.742
But nobody wants to put in the work

00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:48.072
that it takes to win games.

00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:49.765
In the Bible, it talks about in Proverbs,

00:00:49.765 --> 00:00:52.343
it says, "The laborer's
appetite works for him.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:54.780
"And his hunger drives him on.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.891
"The laborer's appetite works for him.

00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:59.062
"And his hunger drives him on."

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:00.695
And so my question to you all is,

00:01:00.695 --> 00:01:02.610
"What's your appetite for winning?"

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.321
Because if you have a
appetite for winning,

00:01:04.321 --> 00:01:05.989
your hunger will drive you, every day.

00:01:05.989 --> 00:01:07.633
Your hunger will take
you to the weight room.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.347
Your hunger will take you past 32.

00:01:09.347 --> 00:01:11.078
Your hunger will take
you past the opposition.

00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:12.854
Your hunger will take you past adversity.

00:01:12.854 --> 00:01:14.999
Your hunger will take you past
the trials and tribulations.

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:16.800
Your hunger will take you
to that fourth quarter

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.002
when there's four zeros on that clock.

00:01:18.002 --> 00:01:19.124
You have emptied that bucket,

00:01:19.124 --> 00:01:21.359
you have given everything
you had, in that game.

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:22.895
See, it's a certain mindset
man, when you attack this thing.

00:01:22.895 --> 00:01:25.450
The game of football,
it's not about skill.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.227
That's what people miss the boat on.

00:01:27.227 --> 00:01:29.402
This game is not about, it
has nothing to do with skill.

00:01:29.402 --> 00:01:31.212
It has nothing to do with a 40 yard pass.

00:01:31.212 --> 00:01:33.470
It has nothing to do with
jumping a 40 inch vertical.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.173
What this game is about, it's about will.

00:01:35.173 --> 00:01:36.006
That's it.

00:01:37.124 --> 00:01:39.106
It's not about skill,
this game is about will.

00:01:39.106 --> 00:01:40.742
And so, the moment that
you make up in your mind.

00:01:40.742 --> 00:01:42.421
The day that you make up in your mind,

00:01:42.421 --> 00:01:43.981
that you are going to
play this game for God

00:01:43.981 --> 00:01:45.267
and give everything you got to it.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.280
You can't help, but to
give everything you got.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.757
And that's the moment that you'll realize

00:01:48.757 --> 00:01:50.628
this game has nothing to do with skill.

00:01:50.628 --> 00:01:53.006
I seen plenty of talented guys fold.

00:01:53.006 --> 00:01:54.817
I seen plenty of talented
guys get hit in the mouth,

00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:55.778
and they did't want it.

00:01:55.778 --> 00:01:57.408
I seen plenty of talented guys get punched

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:58.944
in the face and they
go back to the sideline

00:01:58.944 --> 00:02:00.122
and they stand beside they coach.

00:02:00.122 --> 00:02:01.369
And they don't want it no more.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:02.470
They make up excuses.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.650
I seen plenty of talented guys.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.341
They ran a four in 240 and
bench press 325 pounds.

00:02:06.341 --> 00:02:07.551
When third and one came up,

00:02:07.551 --> 00:02:09.567
they tapped they helmet
to come out of the game.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.520
That has nothing to do with skill.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.332
- Ask yourself, "What
if no one ever bought

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.665
"any of my work?

00:02:15.589 --> 00:02:17.306
"What if I'm never going to sell a book,

00:02:17.306 --> 00:02:20.688
"or publish a book, or a short story?"

00:02:20.688 --> 00:02:23.196
Are you going to continue to write?

00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:25.526
And if the answer is,
"Yes, because I have to."

00:02:25.526 --> 00:02:27.408
then yeah, you are a writer.

00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:29.055
And whether you'll sell
or not I can't know,

00:02:29.055 --> 00:02:32.302
but if there's stories in
you that have to get out,

00:02:32.302 --> 00:02:33.913
and you want to put
them down on the paper,

00:02:33.913 --> 00:02:37.933
whether you ever get the
affirmation of a contract,

00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:39.253
or a book in your hand,

00:02:39.253 --> 00:02:40.994
or being on the best seller list.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.590
If you still have to tell your stories

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:44.255
then you're a writer.

00:02:44.255 --> 00:02:46.407
If you can give it up, then probably

00:02:46.407 --> 00:02:49.033
it would be an act of
sanity to learn accounting

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.350
or something like that.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.072
- How much further can you go?

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.650
- That's a really good question.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.103
And I don't know the answer to that.

00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:57.770
I don't have those types of goals, of,

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.269
"I want this number."

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:01.766
I just have the goal
of, "I want to play well

00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:02.599
"at this tournament.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:03.985
"I want to win this tournament.

00:03:03.985 --> 00:03:05.329
"And then I want to win this tournament."

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:07.238
And when I wake up one morning

00:03:07.238 --> 00:03:09.602
and just, absolutely, do
not want to go on the court.

00:03:09.602 --> 00:03:12.683
Or have no motivation to go on the court,

00:03:12.683 --> 00:03:15.192
then that's when it'll be, good for me.

00:03:15.192 --> 00:03:17.319
- Has acting turned out to be

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:20.160
all that you wanted it to be?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.660
- It's incredible.

00:03:26.697 --> 00:03:30.140
You know, I never knew that
I could do it as a career.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.743
It was the first memory that I had.

00:03:32.743 --> 00:03:35.025
The first thing I could
think of is saying,

00:03:35.025 --> 00:03:36.991
"I want to be an actor, to my parents."

00:03:36.991 --> 00:03:39.668
And if I hadn't lived in Los Angeles

00:03:39.668 --> 00:03:42.057
and been in such close proximity,

00:03:42.057 --> 00:03:45.463
to, sort of, the mecca of movie making,

00:03:45.463 --> 00:03:46.864
if I didn't have parents that said,

00:03:46.864 --> 00:03:48.905
"Okay, we'll drive you to auditions."

00:03:48.905 --> 00:03:50.524
We didn't have the economic means

00:03:50.524 --> 00:03:53.513
to move camp from Idaho to Los Angeles

00:03:53.513 --> 00:03:55.313
because some snotty, 10 year old kid says,

00:03:55.313 --> 00:03:56.431
"I want to be an actor."

00:03:56.431 --> 00:03:57.835
(laughs)

00:03:57.835 --> 00:04:00.043
We did it, after school
I got to go on auditions,

00:04:00.043 --> 00:04:02.095
but it was always, and
I've said this before,

00:04:02.095 --> 00:04:04.372
it felt like an elite group of people.

00:04:04.372 --> 00:04:07.434
And it felt like I would
never belong to them.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:10.973
So once I got the
opportunity to, for example,

00:04:10.973 --> 00:04:12.460
get the movie, This Boy's Life,

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.020
with Robert DeNiro, I said,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:19.001
"Wow, I might be able to
steer the course of my career.

00:04:19.001 --> 00:04:20.203
"I might be able to have a career,

00:04:20.203 --> 00:04:23.620
"similar to these guys that I so admire."

00:04:24.637 --> 00:04:27.150
And that, I knew at 15 years old,

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.119
was the biggest gift in the world.

00:04:29.119 --> 00:04:31.202
And that's never left me.

00:04:33.936 --> 00:04:36.636
That thirst or that hunger, for wanting

00:04:36.636 --> 00:04:38.074
to give one great performance

00:04:38.074 --> 00:04:39.778
that I am truly satisfied with.

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.014
Or be in one movie, that I said,

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:43.860
"I love this film," is something

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.350
that I don't know will ever be quenched.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.405
I don't know.

00:04:47.405 --> 00:04:49.340
And I think that's a good thing.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.876
Because it keeps pushing you, you know?

00:04:52.876 --> 00:04:55.089
Constantly dissatisfied, in other words.

00:04:55.089 --> 00:04:57.893
- Paul Newman told me,
that any successful person,

00:04:57.893 --> 00:05:02.163
in any field, who in
discussing their career,

00:05:02.163 --> 00:05:05.284
doesn't use the word, luck, is a liar.

00:05:05.284 --> 00:05:07.551
- Oh yeah, he's absolutely right.

00:05:07.551 --> 00:05:09.627
- So you consider yourself lucky.

00:05:09.627 --> 00:05:11.163
- Very lucky, yeah.

00:05:11.163 --> 00:05:13.430
- But you have to have talent,
to meet the luck, right?

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:16.635
- Somebody hands you the ball and you run.

00:05:16.635 --> 00:05:19.132
And if you get hit, you get hit.

00:05:19.132 --> 00:05:20.833
Or maybe you make it through.

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.229
You never know.

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:24.950
But I just know that
somebody handed me the ball,

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.244
at a certain point,
and I was hungry enough

00:05:27.244 --> 00:05:28.672
to keep running.

00:05:28.672 --> 00:05:30.665
And I'm still running.

00:05:30.665 --> 00:05:34.498
I've maintained a hunger,
but not an ambition.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:41.152
I'm very happy to
explore all possibilities

00:05:41.152 --> 00:05:43.323
of the character.

00:05:43.323 --> 00:05:44.823
And really dive in

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.060
to the role.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:52.750
I mean, to the point of where
Disney wanted to fire me.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.420
- They wanted to fire you from, Pirates?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.253
- Yeah.

00:05:55.253 --> 00:05:56.504
- Because?

00:05:56.504 --> 00:05:58.374
- They couldn't understand
what I was doing.

00:05:58.374 --> 00:05:59.970
And they didn't understand the character.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.428
They actually were contemplating
subtitling the film.

00:06:03.428 --> 00:06:05.964
(laughs)

00:06:05.964 --> 00:06:07.608
- I mean, success, I
don't think it's something

00:06:07.608 --> 00:06:11.608
you can, I don't think
you can describe success.

00:06:14.793 --> 00:06:17.756
Because it means different
things to different people.

00:06:17.756 --> 00:06:20.840
And there's different levels of success.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.316
I'd say we're starting
to enjoy success now.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.834
I bought my mom a brand
new car for her birthday.

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:29.805
That was definitely a
dream come true, for me.

00:06:29.805 --> 00:06:31.296
That was a level of success.

00:06:31.296 --> 00:06:34.135
But then you look at Jay Z,
you know what I'm saying?

00:06:34.135 --> 00:06:36.095
He'll tell you a billion is success.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.450
When he makes it to a B, or whatever,

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.094
you know what I'm saying?

00:06:39.094 --> 00:06:41.818
He's way, way, way up
there in the stratosphere.

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:45.211
So, that's just, like, I
don't tell myself I made it.

00:06:45.211 --> 00:06:46.712
I don't tell myself I'm successful.

00:06:46.712 --> 00:06:48.046
I tell myself, I'm hungry.

00:06:48.046 --> 00:06:49.366
And I want to keep going.

00:06:49.366 --> 00:06:52.522
- I didn't have an easy experience.

00:06:52.522 --> 00:06:55.964
I didn't come in as a top rated recruit.

00:06:55.964 --> 00:06:58.088
I didn't come in with the opportunity

00:06:58.088 --> 00:06:59.840
to play right away.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:01.700
I had to earn it.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.118
And you know what the greatest honor

00:07:03.118 --> 00:07:06.214
I've ever received, as a player is?

00:07:06.214 --> 00:07:08.119
In my fourth year and my fifth year,

00:07:08.119 --> 00:07:10.641
I was named team captain.

00:07:10.641 --> 00:07:12.751
That, to this day, is the single,

00:07:12.751 --> 00:07:16.918
greatest achievement I've
ever had as a football player.

00:07:18.089 --> 00:07:22.100
Because the men in this room
chose me to lead their team.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.626
And these were my best friends.

00:07:23.626 --> 00:07:27.140
These were the guys that
knew that I liked to work.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:28.734
That knew that I loved football.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.159
That knew that I loved to play.

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:32.504
That knew that I wanted to be

00:07:32.504 --> 00:07:35.708
the quarterback for Michigan.

00:07:35.708 --> 00:07:37.484
And all the lessons that I learnt here

00:07:37.484 --> 00:07:40.462
on State Street, and in the big house.

00:07:40.462 --> 00:07:44.252
That's still what I
bring to practice today.

00:07:44.252 --> 00:07:45.934
And after 14 years, I love the game

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.879
more than I've ever loved it.

00:07:47.879 --> 00:07:49.451
- Oh, it was historical.

00:07:49.451 --> 00:07:51.276
I was thinking about
that run all the time.

00:07:51.276 --> 00:07:55.096
Oklahoma City is all about, first off,

00:07:55.096 --> 00:07:58.708
natural disasters, and
Oklahoma City bombing.

00:07:58.708 --> 00:07:59.990
Just to put it out there, to be real.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.090
That's what this city was known for.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:05.176
And to win, a Western
Conference Championship

00:08:05.176 --> 00:08:06.733
with a group of young guys,

00:08:06.733 --> 00:08:08.880
in a city that's never
seen anything like it,

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.080
that's something I'm
always going to remember.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.940
- [Announcer] But the
Thunder, lost the NBA title

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.670
to the Miami Heat and
LeBron James in five games.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.108
Kevin Durant was second, again.

00:08:19.108 --> 00:08:21.074
And there to console
him was the same person

00:08:21.074 --> 00:08:23.162
who made him do pushups,
in the middle of the night,

00:08:23.162 --> 00:08:24.579
12 years earlier.

00:08:25.452 --> 00:08:27.986
- [Interviewer] A long hug
with your mom, after you all

00:08:27.986 --> 00:08:29.306
didn't make it there.

00:08:29.306 --> 00:08:32.427
You hugged her long and hard.

00:08:32.427 --> 00:08:35.391
- Well first off, that
was just like a thank you.

00:08:35.391 --> 00:08:39.567
My mom, she was always there
at the right time, man.

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:41.079
And a lot of people got on me for crying

00:08:41.079 --> 00:08:42.329
on national TV.

00:08:43.527 --> 00:08:45.468
But, when you wanted something that bad,

00:08:45.468 --> 00:08:47.105
it was just like, I didn't care.

00:08:47.105 --> 00:08:48.338
- I do everything.

00:08:48.338 --> 00:08:50.825
I love jet skiing,
going out on club bikes,

00:08:50.825 --> 00:08:53.043
motorbikes, surfing, rock climbing,

00:08:53.043 --> 00:08:54.926
pretty much anything with an engine.

00:08:54.926 --> 00:08:56.537
Yeah, I try to do as many things as I can.

00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:57.508
I love to do water skiing.

00:08:57.508 --> 00:08:59.835
I like to do wakeboarding
and water skiing.

00:08:59.835 --> 00:09:02.699
I pretty much do quite a few things,

00:09:02.699 --> 00:09:05.111
but those are the things I do to,

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:06.456
My dad will be like,
"You shouldn't be doing

00:09:06.456 --> 00:09:07.462
"any of those things.

00:09:07.462 --> 00:09:08.581
"Because you race a Formula One car,

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:09.768
"you don't need it."

00:09:09.768 --> 00:09:11.113
But when you're not
racing, you need something

00:09:11.113 --> 00:09:13.660
to keep that adrenaline
and that hunger going.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:17.339
- [Man] Get the plague and
the people holding the plaque.

00:09:17.339 --> 00:09:19.141
- [Young Man] Bad boy, represent.

00:09:19.141 --> 00:09:21.280
- [Man] Get the plaque.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.784
Couple of times, on the plaque, aight.

00:09:24.784 --> 00:09:27.184
- We just going to keep trying
to feed our families, yo.

00:09:27.184 --> 00:09:28.017
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:28.017 --> 00:09:28.850
It's a job.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.698
It ain't nothing where somebody just felt

00:09:30.698 --> 00:09:31.645
like doing it and they did it,

00:09:31.645 --> 00:09:32.690
you know what I'm saying?

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:33.937
We was hungry.

00:09:33.937 --> 00:09:35.102
Everybody got to eat,
know what I'm saying?

00:09:35.102 --> 00:09:36.159
I found something I was good at.

00:09:36.159 --> 00:09:38.103
I'm just trying to flip it, yo.

00:09:38.103 --> 00:09:39.064
Keep it going, you know what I'm saying?

00:09:39.064 --> 00:09:40.492
I ain't trying to slack at all.

00:09:40.492 --> 00:09:42.098
I'm a throw this out to my peoples,

00:09:42.098 --> 00:09:45.337
my borough, and my family, and on my eye.

00:09:45.337 --> 00:09:46.347
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:46.347 --> 00:09:47.329
I hope you enjoyed.

00:09:47.329 --> 00:09:48.733
I'd love to know which of the clips

00:09:48.733 --> 00:09:50.655
had the biggest impact on you and why.

00:09:50.655 --> 00:09:51.936
Leave it down in the comments.

00:09:51.936 --> 00:09:53.446
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:09:53.446 --> 00:09:56.556
I also want to know, how
are you being hungry?

00:09:56.556 --> 00:09:58.203
What do you do in your business,

00:09:58.203 --> 00:10:00.422
in your life, right now to stay hungry?

00:10:00.422 --> 00:10:02.149
Leave it down in the comments.

00:10:02.149 --> 00:10:03.253
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:10:03.253 --> 00:10:04.323
to Charli Funk.

00:10:04.323 --> 00:10:05.604
Thank you Charli for picking up a copy

00:10:05.604 --> 00:10:06.879
of my book, Your One Word,

00:10:06.879 --> 00:10:08.283
and sending that Tweet out about it.

00:10:08.283 --> 00:10:10.093
I really, really, really appreciate it.

